{"id":"neuburg-1945-04-26","title":"Neuburg an der Donau, 26 April 1945","short":"Neuburg · 26 April 1945","eyebrow":"","theater":"europe","clock":"B","window":{"from":"1945-04-26T07:15Z","to":"1945-04-26T16:25Z"},"gmt":true,"participants":[{"id":"106aaa-d","name":"Battery D, 106th AAA AW Bn","of":"us","kind":"army","unit":"106aaa-d","basis":"inferred","note":"the battalion fired; Battery D was defending the 189th that month (Where was Battery D?, below)","followed":true,"opposed":false},{"id":"189fa","name":"189th Field Artillery Bn","of":"us","kind":"army","unit":"189fa","note":"watched from Bergen","followed":true,"opposed":false}],"own":["us"],"against":null,"places":[],"sections":[{"heading":"","paras":[{"text":"Me 262 jets attack a formation of B-26s over the Danube at Neuburg, and three records that never mention each other describe the same five minutes: the 106th AAA AW Battalion's history (its batteries fired on the jets), the 189th Field Artillery Battalion's history (it watched from Bergen, just north-west of the town), and the 17th Bomb Group's three Missing Air Crew Reports. The German side so far is secondary: Adolf Galland's last two claims, and published accounts of JV 44's mission.","aside":false},{"text":"Clocks: the Army's B time and German summer time were both UTC+2. The MACRs' times are as typed.","aside":false},{"text":"Still to find: JV 44's own records and the Luftwaffe's loss returns (to name the jets lost); the 17th Bomb Group's mission report (AFHRA); the escorting P-47 group's report; the 45th Division's G-2 periodic report for 26 April; the 106th's journal for the day (`ok45th-17541`, around p. 27).","aside":false}]},{"heading":"Outcome","paras":[{"text":"Three B-26s of the 17th Bomb Group were lost to enemy aircraft over Neuburg between 1145 and 1152, one each from the 34th, 432nd and 37th Squadrons, each with its Missing Air Crew Report [[cite:rg92-91150810/p02]] [[cite:rg92-91150796/p02]] [[cite:rg92-91150835/p02]]. The 106th AAA AW Battalion's history has its Batteries C and D engaging six Me 262s from 1145B to 1147B \"without result\" [[cite:ok45th-17560/p06]]; the 189th Field Artillery Battalion's, watching from Bergen, has four jets, three bombers shot down and \"one of the German aircraft was downed\" [[cite:ok45th-14862/p10]]. Whose fire, if any, brought a jet down, no record read says. The German side is secondary so far: [Galland's two claims that day](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_aerial_victories_claimed_by_Adolf_Galland), and the published accounts of JV 44's mission.","aside":false}]},{"heading":"Sources","paras":[{"text":"The folder's files, for anyone reading the records themselves:","aside":false},{"text":"`claims.yml` uses one more `weight`, `secondary`: a published account, not yet checked against the record it draws on.","aside":false}]}],"cites":{"rg92-91150810/p02":{"href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/id/91150810?objectPage=02","short":"National Archives","title":"National Archives Catalog","page":"02"},"rg92-91150796/p02":{"href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/id/91150796?objectPage=02","short":"National Archives","title":"National Archives Catalog","page":"02"},"rg92-91150835/p02":{"href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/id/91150835?objectPage=02","short":"National Archives","title":"National Archives Catalog","page":"02"},"ok45th-17560/p06":{"href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/17560","short":"ok45th","title":"45th Infantry Division unit histories and journals (the 106th AAA AW Bn's history and journal, July 1944 – May 1945; the 189th FA Bn's history)","page":"06"},"ok45th-14862/p10":{"href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/14862","short":"ok45th","title":"45th Infantry Division unit histories and journals (the 106th AAA AW Bn's history and journal, July 1944 – May 1945; the 189th FA Bn's history)","page":"10"}},"box":[10.509,47.844,12.028,49.55],"steps":[{"id":"s1","utc":"1945-04-26T08:15Z","key":"1945-04-26T08:15Z","local":"1945-04-26 1015","when":"","view":{"name":"","basis":"entries","box":[[10.794,48.484],[11.494,49.084]]},"entries":2},{"id":"s2","utc":"1945-04-26T09:30Z","key":"1945-04-26T09:30Z","local":"1945-04-26 1130","when":"","view":{"name":"","basis":"entries","box":[[10.794,47.844],[12.028,49.084]]},"entries":8},{"id":"s3","utc":"1945-04-26T13:15Z","key":"1945-04-26T13:15Z","local":"1945-04-26 1515","when":"","view":{"name":"","basis":"entries","box":[[10.755,48.484],[11.494,49.118]]},"entries":2}],"relief":[],"roads":"","fronts":[],"stations":{"106aaa-d":[{"date":"1945-04-22","lat":49.2501,"lon":11.0905,"place":"Roth","words":"Roth Coord. T-439776","precision":"","inside":false,"cite":{"ref":"ok45th-17541/p23","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/17541","label":"p. 23","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"}},{"date":"1945-04-23","lat":49.0306,"lon":10.9719,"place":"Weißenburg in Bayern","words":"Weisenberg at T-367330","precision":"","inside":false,"cite":{"ref":"ok45th-17541/p24","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/17541","label":"p. 24","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"}},{"date":"1945-04-25","lat":48.8415,"lon":10.8611,"place":"Monheim (Swabia)","words":"Monheim at T-291315","precision":"","inside":false,"cite":{"ref":"ok45th-17541/p25","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/17541","label":"p. 25","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"}},{"date":"1945-04-26","lat":48.8208,"lon":11.0834,"place":"Wellheim","words":"Wellheim T-455299","precision":"","inside":true,"cite":{"ref":"ok45th-17541/p27","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/17541","label":"p. 27","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"}}],"189fa":[]},"tracks":{},"fixes":[],"events":[{"placed":"The month's assignment; no time","of":"us","actor":"106th AAA AW Bn","kind":"assignment","words":"Battery D's mission for April: \"Defense of 189th Field Artillery Battalion; Defense of 45th Div. Arty. Cub Air Fields\".","source":"106th AAA AW Bn, April 1945 history, p. 2","ref":"ok45th-17560/p02","step":"s1","origin":"events","n":1,"local":"1945-04","utc":null,"key":"1945-04","cite":{"ref":"ok45th-17560/p02","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/17560","label":"p. 2","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"},"outside":false,"opposed":false,"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"of":"us","actor":"189th FA Bn","kind":"move","words":"The battalion moves at 1015 to Bergen, just north-west of Neuburg.","source":"189th FA Bn, April 1945 history, typed pp. 246-247","ref":"ok45th-14862/p10","pos":"bergen","step":"s1","origin":"events","n":2,"local":"1945-04-26 1015","utc":"1945-04-26T08:15Z","key":"1945-04-26T08:15Z","cite":{"ref":"ok45th-14862/p10","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/14862","label":"p. 10","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"},"lat":48.7837,"lon":11.1436,"outside":false,"opposed":false,"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"placed":"Secondary accounts; not yet checked against a German record","of":"de","actor":"JV 44","kind":"launch","words":"Twelve Me 262s of JV 44 take off from Munich-Riem with R4M rockets to attack B-26s.","source":"The Aviation Geek Club, drawing on Robert Forsyth's histories of JV 44","ref":"https://theaviationgeekclub.com/the-b-26-was-usaaf-bomber-luftwaffe-me-262-pilots-would-least-enjoy-to-attack-heres-why/","pos":"riem","step":"s2","origin":"events","n":3,"local":"1945-04-26 1130","utc":"1945-04-26T09:30Z","key":"1945-04-26T09:30Z","cite":{"ref":"https://theaviationgeekclub.com/the-b-26-was-usaaf-bomber-luftwaffe-me-262-pilots-would-least-enjoy-to-attack-heres-why/","href":"https://theaviationgeekclub.com/the-b-26-was-usaaf-bomber-luftwaffe-me-262-pilots-would-least-enjoy-to-attack-heres-why/","label":"page","source_title":"url","kind":"secondary","of":""},"lat":48.144,"lon":11.6778,"outside":false,"opposed":true,"source_kind":"secondary","source_of":""},{"of":"us","actor":"34th Bomb Sq","kind":"loss","words":"B-26B-41 42-43311 \"Spot Cash\", out of Dijon for Lechfeld airfield, lost to \"Enemy Aircraft\". Last known: \"Neuburg, Ger.\". A gunner: \"His ship ... was hit by ME-262's on their first pass\".","source":"Missing Air Crew Report 14163, pp. 2, 4","ref":"rg92-91150810/p02","pos":"spotcash","step":"s2","origin":"events","n":4,"local":"1945-04-26 1145","utc":"1945-04-26T09:45Z","key":"1945-04-26T09:45Z","cite":{"ref":"rg92-91150810/p02","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/id/91150810?objectPage=02","label":"p. 2","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"},"lat":48.7456,"lon":11.188,"outside":false,"opposed":false,"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"of":"us","actor":"106th AAA AW Bn","kind":"engage","words":"\"From 1145B to 1147B six (6) ME-262s flying at 500 to 5000 feet attacking B-26 Bombers were engaged by Batteries C and D without result. Ammunition expenditures: 10 rounds 37mm and 159 rounds .50 cal.\"","source":"106th AAA AW Bn, April 1945 history, p. 6","ref":"ok45th-17560/p06","pos":"bergen","step":"s2","origin":"events","n":5,"local":"1945-04-26 1145","utc":"1945-04-26T09:45Z","key":"1945-04-26T09:45Z","cite":{"ref":"ok45th-17560/p06","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/17560","label":"p. 6","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"},"lat":48.7837,"lon":11.1436,"outside":false,"opposed":false,"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"of":"us","actor":"432nd Bomb Sq","kind":"loss","words":"B-26G-25 44-68076 \"Big Red\" (No. 98) lost to \"Enemy Aircraft\". Last known 48° 46′ N, 11° 11′ E. The squadron's sketch map has the formation heading south-south-east past Eichstätt and the X just north of Neuburg.","source":"Missing Air Crew Report 14162, pp. 2, 5","ref":"rg92-91150796/p02","pos":"bigred","step":"s2","origin":"events","n":6,"local":"1945-04-26 1150","utc":"1945-04-26T09:50Z","key":"1945-04-26T09:50Z","cite":{"ref":"rg92-91150796/p02","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/id/91150796?objectPage=02","label":"p. 2","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"},"lat":48.7667,"lon":11.1833,"outside":false,"opposed":false,"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"placed":"A claim as tabulated from a secondary source","of":"de","actor":"JV 44","kind":"claim","words":"Generalleutnant Adolf Galland, commanding JV 44, claims a B-26 \"vicinity of Neuburg\": his 100th, credited. It was his last mission.","source":"Mathews and Foreman, Luftwaffe Aces, vol. 2, p. 366, as tabulated in Wikipedia","ref":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_aerial_victories_claimed_by_Adolf_Galland","pos":"neuburg","step":"s2","origin":"events","n":7,"local":"1945-04-26 1150","utc":"1945-04-26T09:50Z","key":"1945-04-26T09:50Z","cite":{"ref":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_aerial_victories_claimed_by_Adolf_Galland","href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_aerial_victories_claimed_by_Adolf_Galland","label":"page","source_title":"url","kind":"secondary","of":""},"lat":48.7456,"lon":11.188,"outside":false,"opposed":true,"source_kind":"secondary","source_of":""},{"of":"us","actor":"37th Bomb Sq","kind":"loss","words":"B-26F 42-96328 (No. 25), typed \"B26-F1MA\", lost to \"Enemy Aircraft\". Last known \"Neuberg, Germany\". A gunner: \"It was attacked by a ME-262 from 6 o'clock level ... flames enveloped the ship from cockpit to rear bomb bay\". The squadron's sketch map puts it down in the woods at Rohrenfels, south of the Danube.","source":"Missing Air Crew Report 14164, pp. 2, 5-6","ref":"rg92-91150835/p02","pos":"rohrenfels","step":"s2","origin":"events","n":8,"local":"1945-04-26 1152","utc":"1945-04-26T09:52Z","key":"1945-04-26T09:52Z","cite":{"ref":"rg92-91150835/p02","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/id/91150835?objectPage=02","label":"p. 2","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"},"lat":48.6862,"lon":11.1565,"outside":false,"opposed":false,"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"placed":"A claim as tabulated from a secondary source","of":"de","actor":"JV 44","kind":"claim","words":"Galland claims a second B-26 \"vicinity of Neuburg\", unconfirmed.","source":"Mathews and Foreman, Luftwaffe Aces, vol. 2, p. 366, as tabulated in Wikipedia","ref":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_aerial_victories_claimed_by_Adolf_Galland","pos":"neuburg","step":"s2","origin":"events","n":9,"local":"1945-04-26 1155","utc":"1945-04-26T09:55Z","key":"1945-04-26T09:55Z","cite":{"ref":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_aerial_victories_claimed_by_Adolf_Galland","href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_aerial_victories_claimed_by_Adolf_Galland","label":"page","source_title":"url","kind":"secondary","of":""},"lat":48.7456,"lon":11.188,"outside":false,"opposed":true,"source_kind":"secondary","source_of":""},{"placed":"A round number","of":"us","actor":"189th FA Bn","kind":"witness","words":"\"At 1200 we witnessed a sad sight. A formation of American bombers flying directly overhead were attacked by four German jet propelled planes, and three of the bombers were shot down, one of which burst into flame and exploded in the air. One of the German aircraft was downed but the rest got away.\"","source":"189th FA Bn, April 1945 history, typed pp. 246-247","ref":"ok45th-14862/p10","pos":"bergen","step":"s2","origin":"events","n":10,"local":"1945-04-26 1200","utc":"1945-04-26T10:00Z","key":"1945-04-26T10:00Z","cite":{"ref":"ok45th-14862/p10","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/14862","label":"p. 10","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"},"lat":48.7837,"lon":11.1436,"outside":false,"opposed":false,"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"of":"us","actor":"106th AAA AW Bn","kind":"move","words":"The battalion's command post opens at Wellheim at 1515B.","source":"106th AAA AW Bn journal, p. 27","ref":"ok45th-17541/p27","pos":"wellheim","step":"s3","origin":"events","n":11,"local":"1945-04-26 1515","utc":"1945-04-26T13:15Z","key":"1945-04-26T13:15Z","cite":{"ref":"ok45th-17541/p27","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/17541","label":"p. 27","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"},"lat":48.8183,"lon":11.1047,"outside":false,"opposed":false,"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"of":"us","actor":"106th AAA AW Bn","kind":"engage","words":"A single Me 262 is engaged again by Batteries C and D, also without result.","source":"106th AAA AW Bn, April 1945 history, p. 6","ref":"ok45th-17560/p06","pos":"bergen","step":"s3","origin":"events","n":12,"local":"1945-04-26 1725","utc":"1945-04-26T15:25Z","key":"1945-04-26T15:25Z","cite":{"ref":"ok45th-17560/p06","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/17560","label":"p. 6","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"},"lat":48.7837,"lon":11.1436,"outside":false,"opposed":false,"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"}],"claims":[{"question":"When?","answer":"1145 to 1147","weight":"record","source":"106th AAA AW Bn history, p. 6","ref":"ok45th-17560/p06","note":"The battery's engagement: two minutes","cite":{"ref":"ok45th-17560/p06","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/17560","label":"p. 6","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"},"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"question":"When?","answer":"1145, 1150 and 1152","weight":"record","source":"Missing Air Crew Reports 14163, 14162, 14164","ref":"rg92-91150796/p02","note":"The time each bomber was lost","cite":{"ref":"rg92-91150796/p02","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/id/91150796?objectPage=02","label":"p. 2","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"},"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"question":"When?","answer":"1150 and 1155","weight":"secondary","source":"Galland's claims (Mathews and Foreman, via Wikipedia)","ref":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_aerial_victories_claimed_by_Adolf_Galland","note":"German summer time and the Army's B time were both UTC+2: no conversion","cite":{"ref":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_aerial_victories_claimed_by_Adolf_Galland","href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_aerial_victories_claimed_by_Adolf_Galland","label":"page","source_title":"url","kind":"secondary","of":""},"source_kind":"secondary","source_of":""},{"question":"When?","answer":"\"At 1200\"","weight":"record","source":"189th FA Bn history, typed p. 246","ref":"ok45th-14862/p10","note":"A round number","cite":{"ref":"ok45th-14862/p10","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/14862","label":"p. 10","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"},"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"question":"When?","answer":"\"Approximately five minutes before reaching the target\"","weight":"recollection","source":"Big Red's co-pilot, MACR 14162 p. 9","ref":"rg92-91150796/p09","cite":{"ref":"rg92-91150796/p09","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/id/91150796?objectPage=09","label":"p. 9","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"},"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"question":"How many jets?","answer":"Six","weight":"record","source":"106th AAA AW Bn history, p. 6","ref":"ok45th-17560/p06","cite":{"ref":"ok45th-17560/p06","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/17560","label":"p. 6","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"},"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"question":"How many jets?","answer":"Four","weight":"record","source":"189th FA Bn history, typed p. 246","ref":"ok45th-14862/p10","cite":{"ref":"ok45th-14862/p10","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/14862","label":"p. 10","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"},"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"question":"How many jets?","answer":"\"Two German Jet-Propelled Fighters\"","weight":"recollection","source":"Big Red's pilot, 1st Lt. Alf P. Shatto, November 1945, MACR 14162 p. 10","ref":"rg92-91150796/p10","note":"What attacked his own aircraft","cite":{"ref":"rg92-91150796/p10","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/id/91150796?objectPage=10","label":"p. 10","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"},"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"question":"How many jets?","answer":"Twelve took off","weight":"secondary","source":"The Aviation Geek Club, after Forsyth","ref":"https://theaviationgeekclub.com/the-b-26-was-usaaf-bomber-luftwaffe-me-262-pilots-would-least-enjoy-to-attack-heres-why/","note":"JV 44's whole formation","cite":{"ref":"https://theaviationgeekclub.com/the-b-26-was-usaaf-bomber-luftwaffe-me-262-pilots-would-least-enjoy-to-attack-heres-why/","href":"https://theaviationgeekclub.com/the-b-26-was-usaaf-bomber-luftwaffe-me-262-pilots-would-least-enjoy-to-attack-heres-why/","label":"page","source_title":"url","kind":"secondary","of":""},"source_kind":"secondary","source_of":""},{"question":"How many bombers were lost?","answer":"Three","weight":"record","source":"Missing Air Crew Reports 14162-14164","ref":"rg92-91150810/p02","note":"One each from the 34th, 432nd and 37th squadrons","cite":{"ref":"rg92-91150810/p02","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/id/91150810?objectPage=02","label":"p. 2","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"},"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"question":"How many bombers were lost?","answer":"\"Three of the bombers were shot down\"","weight":"record","source":"189th FA Bn history, typed p. 246","ref":"ok45th-14862/p10","cite":{"ref":"ok45th-14862/p10","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/14862","label":"p. 10","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"},"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"question":"How many bombers were lost?","answer":"Five claimed","weight":"secondary","source":"The Aviation Geek Club, after Forsyth","ref":"https://theaviationgeekclub.com/the-b-26-was-usaaf-bomber-luftwaffe-me-262-pilots-would-least-enjoy-to-attack-heres-why/","note":"JV 44's claims, including Galland's two","cite":{"ref":"https://theaviationgeekclub.com/the-b-26-was-usaaf-bomber-luftwaffe-me-262-pilots-would-least-enjoy-to-attack-heres-why/","href":"https://theaviationgeekclub.com/the-b-26-was-usaaf-bomber-luftwaffe-me-262-pilots-would-least-enjoy-to-attack-heres-why/","label":"page","source_title":"url","kind":"secondary","of":""},"source_kind":"secondary","source_of":""},{"question":"Was a jet brought down?","answer":"\"One of the German aircraft was downed\"","weight":"record","source":"189th FA Bn history, typed p. 246","ref":"ok45th-14862/p10","cite":{"ref":"ok45th-14862/p10","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/14862","label":"p. 10","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"},"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"question":"Was a jet brought down?","answer":"\"Without result\"","weight":"record","source":"106th AAA AW Bn history, p. 6","ref":"ok45th-17560/p06","note":"The 106th's own claim for its fire. Nobody's record says whose fire hit which jet","cite":{"ref":"ok45th-17560/p06","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/17560","label":"p. 6","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"},"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"question":"Was a jet brought down?","answer":"Two JV 44 pilots lost","weight":"secondary","source":"The Aviation Geek Club, after Forsyth","ref":"https://theaviationgeekclub.com/the-b-26-was-usaaf-bomber-luftwaffe-me-262-pilots-would-least-enjoy-to-attack-heres-why/","note":"One bailed out. Galland, wounded, crash-landed at Riem after a P-47 hit him","cite":{"ref":"https://theaviationgeekclub.com/the-b-26-was-usaaf-bomber-luftwaffe-me-262-pilots-would-least-enjoy-to-attack-heres-why/","href":"https://theaviationgeekclub.com/the-b-26-was-usaaf-bomber-luftwaffe-me-262-pilots-would-least-enjoy-to-attack-heres-why/","label":"page","source_title":"url","kind":"secondary","of":""},"source_kind":"secondary","source_of":""},{"question":"Whose flak?","answer":"\"We were also being fired upon by a German Anti-Aircraft Battery\"","weight":"recollection","source":"Shatto, MACR 14162 p. 10","ref":"rg92-91150796/p10","cite":{"ref":"rg92-91150796/p10","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/id/91150796?objectPage=10","label":"p. 10","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"},"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"question":"Whose flak?","answer":"The front was the Danube","weight":"inference","source":"The 106th's positions; the MACRs' sketch maps","ref":"ok45th-17541/p27","note":"German flak south of the river, the 45th Division's guns north of it. Either could have been firing at the bombers' altitude","cite":{"ref":"ok45th-17541/p27","href":"https://cdm17494.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/ok45th/id/17541","label":"p. 27","source_title":"ok45th","kind":"record","of":"us"},"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"question":"Where did Big Red come down?","answer":"48° 46′ N, 11° 11′ E","weight":"record","source":"MACR 14162, p. 2","ref":"rg92-91150796/p02","cite":{"ref":"rg92-91150796/p02","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/id/91150796?objectPage=02","label":"p. 2","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"},"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"question":"Where did Big Red come down?","answer":"Just north of Neuburg","weight":"record","source":"MACR 14162, p. 5 (sketch map)","ref":"rg92-91150796/p05","note":"Agrees with the form","cite":{"ref":"rg92-91150796/p05","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/id/91150796?objectPage=05","label":"p. 5","source_title":"National Archives","kind":"record","of":"us"},"source_kind":"record","source_of":"us"},{"question":"Where did Big Red come down?","answer":"\"About four to six miles southwest of Ulm\"","weigh